{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "pmat",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "pmat analyze complexity --file (CLI transport); pmat query --literal; pmat index rebuild at HEAD"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "pmat.complexity-new-files",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cognitive complexity of two new Rust files that carry real logic: crates/aprender-contracts/src/discharge/mod.rs max cognitive 11 (judge_escapes), max cyclomatic 8, 30 functions; crates/aprender-common/src/cli_roles.rs max cognitive 2, 22 functions. Both are below the configured max_complexity 10 on cyclomatic; the cognitive 11 is one function. Only these two of the 185 changed .rs files were measured. stdout_sha256 is the discharge/mod.rs run."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "pmat",
              "analyze",
              "complexity",
              "--file",
              "crates/aprender-contracts/src/discharge/mod.rs",
              "--format",
              "json"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "8c0669419351c734dc8750c72937ca28909152c9348ac7faf6429e2cc747ed1a",
            "failure_scenario": "A cognitive-11 judge_escapes in the discharge judge is the hardest function to reason about in a PR that gates lean proofs; growth past it would slip in unmeasured because the other 183 .rs files were not measured.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "pmat.duplication-scan-incomplete",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "pr_review_duplication_scan.sh was started and ran over 14 minutes (a giant git grep -w -F needle list); a --horizon none retry timed out at 110 s. No scan result is recorded. Instead a manual name check of the PR's new tool names against the tree found no prior art: the nearest, scripts/check_shell_lint_ratchet.sh, is a different tool. Every surface is therefore recorded as duplication method none, and the sibling-branch sweep as 0 of 1173 scanned."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "The manual check is a human-shaped grep over a handful of names, not the scan; it cannot stand for the semantic search.",
            "failure_scenario": "A duplicate of an existing guard or of a sibling branch's work would not be found; the PR adds ~10 new scripts/ci helpers and a new pv discharge/challenge/ontology surface.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "pmat.index-stale-later",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The pmat index was rebuilt at HEAD in this worktree (93542 functions, 50.2 s) and the first queries used it. A later pmat query in the same session reported the index stale (context.db written after context.idx/manifest.json) and began a rebuild that did not finish in the 100 s allowed. The index files are gitignored. TDG and SATD were not measured for this PR."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Recording what happened; nothing was inferred from the stale index.",
            "failure_scenario": "Any pmat answer cited from the index after the first queries would describe a database the manifest does not match.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review.delta-kani-harness-property-unchanged",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Reviewed d3991868d2 against witness.rs. accepted_verdict_is_semantic_u8 now takes the verdict; the two Kani harnesses (KANI-ONT-9-1 core and model halves) pass check_u8(&g, &core_as(..)) / check_u8(&g, &model_as(..)), which is exactly the expression the old body computed internally. check_u8 is pub in witness_small.rs and is added to the harness import list. The property (an accepted core is contradictory and names known variables; an accepted model satisfies the graph) is unchanged, and the proptest twin passes the same check_string/check_u8 calls. The new refuses_an_unsound_verdict test hands it hand-built unsound verdicts (core on a satisfiable graph, model on an unsatisfiable one, empty core, id 3 == VARS.len()), so the predicate is no longer indistinguishable from true."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Read from the diff and source only; Kani and the tests were not run here (no cargo on this host).",
            "failure_scenario": "If check_u8 were not pub or the harness import were wrong, the cfg(kani) build would fail to compile; kani is not built by workspace-test, so a break there would surface only in the Kani job.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review.delta-tests-not-executed-here",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Delta 5dfa5e7715..d3991868d2 is 14 files: 11 test/refactor files under aprender-contracts plus README.md, contracts/census.json and contracts.nt (census regen, n_files 1860, contract_count 1860, consistent with each other). No new test asserts a constant: the count_allowlisted, emit_all, semantic, shapes_gate and code.rs tests assert exact values or a both-ways predicate. Whether they kill the CI MISSED mutants is not established here: the scoped local cargo-mutants units a07-m4587p and a07-m4587b were still running when this receipt was written and were not read."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Adversarial read of git diff 5dfa5e7715 HEAD; no test or mutation output consumed.",
            "failure_scenario": "A test that reads as a kill but does not would leave a survivor; the CI mutants shards are the gate for that, not this receipt.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review.delta-step-as-checked-sub",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "step_as now uses checked_sub(3): code<3 gives Unit(id(code)), otherwise Implies(IMPLY_PAIRS[(code-3)%6]). This is the same mapping as the old k<3 / (k-3)%6 form for every u8 code. New tests pin codes 3..8 to the six pairs in order, and step_as(9)==step_as(3) for the wrap."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Read from the diff and source only; not executed here.",
            "failure_scenario": "A regression in the wrap (e.g. removing %6) would index IMPLY_PAIRS out of range for code >= 9; STEP_CODES bounds the harness to 0..9 so Kani would not see it, only the new test does.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review.delta-inline-mod-test-negative-only",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "an_inline_mod_is_not_a_file_backed_child_that_includes_a_sibling asserts only resolve(\"k::inc\",\"f\").is_err(). The fixture shape (workspace Cargo.toml, k/Cargo.toml with [package] name only) matches the neighbouring passing tests, but the test has no positive twin in the same body: an error for any other reason (a scan failure, a wrong path) would also satisfy it, so it kills the targeted mutant only if the fixture scans."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Adversarial read of crates/aprender-contracts/src/ontology/extract/code.rs at HEAD; the mutant is CI's to confirm.",
            "failure_scenario": "If Workspace::scan skipped the fixture, is_err() would hold with the mutant applied and the survivor would remain MISSED in the CI shard.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review.delta-binary-control-bare-sample-orphans",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "the_positive_control_refuses_a_third_apr asserts that clearing every target's commands makes positive_control false because 'apr run' becomes a second orphan (the tightened conjunct is ledgerOrphan.len() == 1 on the second node). Whether both orphans land on that node depends on emit_all's orphan attribution, which this review read but did not execute."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Not executed: cargo test is forbidden on this host.",
            "failure_scenario": "If orphans attach elsewhere or only once, the second assertion would fail in CI (a red test, not a vacuous one).",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "nvidia-cuda-docs",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "mcp__nvidia-cuda-docs__search_cuda_docs x2 (inline; cuda-docs-reviewer agent not dispatched)"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "cuda.trigger-false-positive",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "--match-path fires for 2 changed paths, both under crates/aprender-contracts-staging/lean/Challenge/ (fp8-interchange-v1.lean and its sibling). They are Lean challenge statements whose theorems are all `:= sorry`; they run no device code. Two queries were run inline (the cuda-docs-reviewer agent was not dispatched). The first, on FP8 conversion and saturation, returned the CUDA Math API fp8 conversion reference. The second returned the PTX ISA alternate-format definitions quoted here. Whether the Lean statement's NaN and infinity claims agree with this text was not checked."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "source": "nvidia-cuda-docs search_cuda_docs, PTX ISA 5.2 alternate floating-point data formats",
            "excerpt": "`e4m3` data format:\n:   This data format is an 8-bit floating point format with 4 bits for exponent and 3 bits for\n    mantissa. The `e4m3` encoding does not support infinity and `NaN` values are limited to\n    `0x7f` and `0xff`.",
            "excerpt_sha256": "f7c2dd6c0f558aceb30a46e2ee78fd96c8e48b26639f62578971a6103af345b2",
            "failure_scenario": "If the fp8-interchange Lean statement later is discharged with a NaN encoding other than 0x7f/0xff for e4m3, the proof would certify a format the hardware does not use.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "crux",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "guard predicate --match-crux-surface over the changed pv CLI surface; no crux contract read"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "crux.no-contract-covers-surface",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The diff adds new pv subcommands and flags (discharge, challenge, ontology, role surfaces in crates/aprender-contracts-cli/src/cli.rs). No crux contract was read for them. That is recorded as coverage none; no comparative claim is made and no gap is opened or closed."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Recorded as a finding per S3.C; nothing was measured against a competing tool.",
            "failure_scenario": "A comparative claim about pv against another prover CLI added later would have no crux contract behind it.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "cargo-mutants",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": false,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": [
            {
              "level": "error",
              "message": {
                "text": "cargo mutants was not attempted (attempted=0). The hard rules for this review forbid cargo test, nextest and cargo-mutants on this host (lambda). The diff changes 185 .rs files, so the mutation consultation is triggered and unreachable; the PR's own CI mutants jobs, including the survivor-table gate this PR adds, are the only measurement. Cargo-free guard mutation sets that WERE run are recorded as results below."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "cargo-free.guard-mutation-and-selftests",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cargo-free checks re-run at write time on the disposable-free worktree at head: mutate_lean_modules_reachable_guard.sh scored 18/18 mutants killed; mutate_leanchecker_scoped_guard.sh scored 31/31. Recorded under the cargo-mutants driver only for lack of a better home: they are guard mutation sets for two new shell guards, not cargo-mutants on Rust. stdout_sha256 is the 31/31 run."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "scripts/mutate_leanchecker_scoped_guard.sh"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "e2568a76e305ad78d3d9caa57909546aacdf808076f2390a51d9ce601fd58ef9",
            "failure_scenario": "These sets cover two guards only; the Python survivor-table checker and the Rust code have no mutation measurement here.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "cargo-free.selftest",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Self-test, rc 0: survivor-table gate rule: planted weak rules turn the table RED."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
